# Go style policy ({{.Config.Style}})

Rubric manages this file. Rules apply in this order:

1. The project overrides below.
2. [Go Code Review Comments](https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments).
3. The [Formatting and style section of Go: Best Practices for Production Environments](https://peter.bourgon.org/go-in-production/#formatting-and-style).
4. The [Uber Go Style Guide](https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md), where compatible with the above.

## Overrides

- Do not add explanatory inline or trailing comments in Go code.
- Exported application symbols require documentation comments.
- A declaration's documentation comment has at most two physical lines, each containing at most
  150 Unicode characters, including its comment delimiter.

## Exclusions

- Build constraints (`//go:build`) and Go directives such as `//go:embed` and `//go:generate` are required by tools;
  they are not explanatory comments or declaration documentation.
- Recognized third-party generated code (files marked `// Code generated ... DO NOT EDIT.`) keeps its generator-owned comments.
- Test functions are not exported application API merely because their names start with `Test`.

## Formatting

Format with `gofmt`. Line length is a readability guideline, not a hard limit.
Passing lint does not prove every subjective recommendation in these guides was followed.
